   })                };            </script>        </div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\na. $MPS = 1 - 0.6 = 0.4$.\nb. Multiplier $= 1/MPS = 1/0.4 = 2.5$.\nc. Total change in income $= \\$80\\text{M} \\times 2.5 = \\$200$ million.\nd. Round 1: $80.00$ million (the initial spending). Round 2: $80 \\times 0.6 = \\$48.00$ million.\n   Round 3: $48.00 \\times 0.6 = \\$28.80$ million. Round 4: $28.80 \\times 0.6 \\approx \\$17.28$\n   million. Each round is smaller than the last, since some of each round's income leaks into\n   saving rather than being re-spent.\ne. *Smaller.* A lower MPC of 0.4 means a higher MPS of 0.6, a smaller multiplier of $1/0.6 \\approx\n   1.67$, and a total impact of only $80 \\times 1.67 \\approx \\$133.3$ million, well below the\n   $\\$200$ million in part (c). More of each round leaks into saving instead of being re-spent.\n\n</details>\n\n",
